Process the microphone in the channels a voice is sent in

What the microphone records goes only to the microphone's own sources; a shared screen's
sound comes from a custom source of its own and never passes through the audio
processing. The transport still processed the microphone in the most channels any
sending stream had (AudioState::UpdateAudioTransportWithSendingStreams passes their
maximum): when a screen's sound started going out in stereo, the microphone was
processed in two channels (AudioTransportImpl::RecordedDataIsAvailable, then
AudioProcessingImpl::MaybeInitializeCapture, which initializes the processing again for
a new stream format), and in one again when it stopped. Each time the echo canceller
and the gain control started anew: the sharer's voice went out about 10 dB weaker while
its screen's sound went out, and the others' voices came back as echo for the first
seconds. The microphone is now processed in one channel always; the screen's sound stays
stereo. Tested by test/custom_audio_transport.test.cc.

